p2pool: fork 13 (block major version 6) and fork-index signalling

Base: kryptokrona/p2pool 8edf632fae7ebcbb29d3525144ac77b0dbd6477e ("Increment patch
version to 2"). Apply from the checkout root with `patch -p1 < 0001-fork13-v6.patch`.
Notes: p2pool/README.md in the xkr repository.

* coin_config.h: XKR_FORK13_HEIGHT (compile-time, default 2700000 = xkrd's FORK_13_HEIGHT_MAINNET),
  FORK13_MAJOR_VERSION = 6, SUPPORTED_FORK_INDEX = 13.
* SideChain::network_major_version: major version 6 from block F + 1 on (the hardforks
  tables stop at 5, so without this every v6 share of a peer fails the parser's major
  version check and the peer is disconnected). SideChain::configure_forks reads the
  environment variable XKR_FORK13_HEIGHT only when the daemon reports testnet (called from
  parse_get_info_rpc, before the P2P server and the block cache start).
* BlockTemplate::update: the block minor version is the supported fork index (13) instead
  of Monero's HARDFORK_SUPPORTED_VERSION (16), so xkrd's fork_readiness counts p2pool
  blocks. Not consensus anywhere (kryptokronad, xkrd and the p2pool parser accept any minor
  version <= 127); this is the one intended change before the fork. Also logs an error when
  the daemon's major version disagrees with the local fork table.
* Below the fork height nothing else changes: same coinbase, same block layout, same parser
  rules (the minor-version byte enters the aux hash and sidechain id, which peers recompute
  from the received blob).

